-- title:
--   p-power multiple of an integral weight-2 cusp form as a differential
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N$, a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, and a ring embedding $\iota_0 \colon \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$. Write $R =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ with $X$ integral, and let $\mathcal V$ be a two-chart affine cover of $X$: affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ and $U_0 \cap U_1$ affine. The further data are: a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb Q$ of the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` (the subfield of $\mathbb Q$-Laurent series generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid N$) together with an isomorphism $e_0$ of $M_0.C$ with the fibre $X_{\mathbb Q}$ over the base, whose generic point lies over $U_0$; a ring map $\iota \colon \Gamma(X, U_0) \to$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` (the field generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the former) which sends a section to the coefficientwise image of its germ at the generic point read through $M_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}$, and which is compatible with the structure maps from $R$; the additive map `res` sending $\omega$ in the Čech $H^0$ of the Kähler sections of the cover (the kernel of $\Omega[\Gamma(X,U_0)] \times \Omega[\Gamma(X,U_1)] \to \Omega[\Gamma(X,U_0 \cap U_1)]$) to the image of its first component under the semilinear Kähler map along $(R \to \overline{\mathbb Q}, \iota)$; an $R$-point $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $X$ and a $\mathbb Q$-point $y$ of the fibre lying on it, hitting a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the $q$-adic cusp `cuspInftyFull N`; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` identified with the geometric generic fibre, whose point-to-place bijection is equivariant for the Galois action `arithmeticGalois` and whose places restrict to those of $M_0$ along $\overline{\mathbb Q} \otimes_{\mathbb Q} F_N \cong$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N`; and, for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p \in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$, a lift $\rho$ of $R \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ to $A$, a curve model $M_s$ over the residue field of $A$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC`, identified with the corresponding fibre of $c$, and (when that residue field is algebraically closed) a reduction map $r$ on places satisfying `IsPlaceReductionModL` and compatible with reduction of points. Then for every $f$ in [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3), the $\mathbb Z$-span of the weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers, there are $m \in \mathbb N$ and $\omega$ in that Čech $H^0$ with $\iota_0$ applied coefficientwise to the $q$-expansion `diffQExpBar N (res ω)` equal to $p^m$ times the $q$-expansion of $f$, as Laurent series over $\mathbb C$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-zero half of the integral $q$-expansion principle for the smooth proper relative curve $X$ over $R$: every integral weight-$2$ cusp form on $\Gamma_0(N)$ becomes, after multiplication by a power of $p$, the $q$-expansion of a global relative differential computed from the two-chart Čech complex. It is used by the refinement that removes the $p$-power factor, and through it feeds the comparison of the $p$-adic étale realisation of the modular curve with the space of cusp forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_pow_smul_kaehlerH0_coeffMap_diffQExpBar_eq_qExpansion_of_mem_intLattice_of_ratCurveModel_of_cuspSection_compat_of_neZero.lean

